Give the last-resort font fallback a family Haiku actually has.

`FontCache::GetLastResortFallbackFont()` tries the generic family, then "Sans",
then "Arial". Haiku has none of them, and the function returning null is not a
cosmetic failure. Without a last resort, `FontFallbackList` has no primary
font, `ComputedStyle::GetFontHeight()` takes its `NOTREACHED()` and returns a
zero `FontHeight`, and every line box on the page collapses to nothing.

What that looks like, measured on the VAIO (2026-09-22):

	<span> at 22px            162x0      height zero
	<input> at 22px, pad 5    294x14     = 0 + 10 padding + 4 border
	the same with line-height:30px   294x44
	the same with height:40px        294x54

So a text form control is padding and border around a zero-height inner
editor: it cannot show its value, typed characters go nowhere visible, and
`<pre>` lines draw on top of each other because every line box is at the same
y. Chasing this as "typing does not work" cost most of a day; the give-away is
that naming an explicit `line-height` restores the box, which says the
font-derived height is what is missing. `computed_style.cc(1683)` fires ten or
eleven times on a page with a handful of elements.

Note that a fontconfig alias does not fix it. Substitution rules mapping
Arial, Helvetica and Times onto the Noto families -- including strong
`binding="same"` edits, not just `<alias><prefer>` -- left the measurements
unchanged, because Skia rejects a match whose family name differs from the one
asked for. The fix has to name a family that is really installed.

Noto is what `assets/rchromium-fonts.conf` points fontconfig at and what
`install.sh` requires, so it is the right name here; DejaVu is tried after it
for a machine that has one and not the other.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/skia/font_cache_skia.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/skia/font_cache_skia.cc
@@ -137,6 +137,34 @@
     font_platform_data = GetFontPlatformData(description, arial_creation_params,
                                              AlternateFontName::kLastResort);
   }
+#if defined(OS_HAIKU)
+  // Neither "Sans" nor "Arial" exists on Haiku, and this function returning
+  // null is not a cosmetic failure: FontFallbackList has no primary font,
+  // ComputedStyle::GetFontHeight() takes its NOTREACHED() and returns a zero
+  // FontHeight, and every line box on the page collapses. Measured on the
+  // VAIO: a 22px <span> reports height 0, a 22px <input> reports 294x14 --
+  // padding and border with a zero-height inner editor -- so form controls
+  // cannot be seen or typed into, and <pre> lines draw on top of each other.
+  //
+  // Name a family this machine actually has. The installer requires the Noto
+  // set (assets/rchromium-fonts.conf points fontconfig at
+  // /boot/system/data/fonts), so if this misses there is nothing left to try.
+  if (!font_platform_data) {
+    DEFINE_THREAD_SAFE_STATIC_LOCAL(const FontFaceCreationParams,
+                                    noto_creation_params,
+                                    (AtomicString("Noto Sans")));
+    font_platform_data = GetFontPlatformData(description, noto_creation_params,
+                                             AlternateFontName::kLastResort);
+  }
+  if (!font_platform_data) {
+    DEFINE_THREAD_SAFE_STATIC_LOCAL(const FontFaceCreationParams,
+                                    dejavu_creation_params,
+                                    (AtomicString("DejaVu Sans")));
+    font_platform_data = GetFontPlatformData(
+        description, dejavu_creation_params, AlternateFontName::kLastResort);
+  }
+#endif
+
 #if defined(OS_WIN)
   // Try some more Windows-specific fallbacks.
   if (!font_platform_data) {
